   1834  f4f8							; Room exit handlers — check connection table, switch rooms, reposition player
   1835  f4f8							; ==============================================================================
   1836  f4f8							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1837  f4f8							; C3 (2026-10-20): the four handlers MOVED to bank2 ($FC4F cluster) — the
   1838  f4f8							; connection table is level data in bank2, so each handler now reads its own
   1839  f4f8							; 2-byte conn record directly (bank1 GetConnIdx + FoldIndirect hops gone).
   1840  f4f8							; bank0 keeps only the entry pads at $FBD9-$FBE4 (3 B each, `sta $1FF6`;
   1841  f4f8							; bank2 serves the `jmp` at A+3). The OPPOSITE-EDGE placement is written
   1842  f4f8							; BEFORE `jmp EnterRoomB2`, because EnterRoom never touches RoomX/RoomY
   1843  f4f8							; (checked: EnterRoomB2 + B3RoomBlocks read neither) — that keeps the whole
   1844  f4f8							; tail in bank2 with 0 pushes: EnterRoomB2's `jmp ReturnPad` pops the
   1845  f4f8							; ORIGINAL `jsr ExitRoomXxx` frame, exactly like the old in-bank return.
   1846  f4f8							; Guard: verify_build.CORRIDOR_PADS (4 pads) + check_exit_handlers (edge
   1847  f4f8							; placement precedes the EnterRoomB2 tail; no-exit path ends in ReturnPad).
   1848  f4f8							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
