   2380  f756							; NO REFP1 write here (2026-10-22): REFP1 is ONE register for GRP1, but a
   2381  f756							; frame can draw TWO objects (band pairing, or the 1-of-2 rotation). Driving
   2382  f756							; it from the ACTIVE object made the mirrored miner flip sides every other
   2383  f756							; frame in any room that also had another object. The miner's mirror is
   2384  f756							; gone (a design-based mirror like the LAMP's type 13 needs 32 more art
   2385  f756							; bytes and the table ends 6 B below the $F8C0 pin), so every GRP1 object
   2386  f756							; is drawn unmirrored and REFP1 stays 0 — the bank1 HUD writes 0 for its
   2387  f756							; score, which is exactly what the cave wants.
   2388  f756							; Set ObjTop for kernel GRP1 visibility check.
   2389  f756							; S2.2: ObjTop stored RoomY-relative (ObjTopRel = ActiveObjectY-RoomY+1) so
   2390  f756							; the kernel compares against running-Y (`tya`) instead of `lda Scanline`
   2391  f756							; — frees 9c/line (lda Scanline + inc Scanline) for the laser beam write.
   2392  f756							; Kernel .Grp1 does: tya / sec / sbc ObjTop / cmp #OBJ_WINDOW / bcs.
   2393  f756							; ObjBot (write-only, no readers): stores removed S1.5, decl removed
   2394  f756							; S3.0b (was last sequential decl — no address shift).
