   2462  f79b							; The frame's ONE HMOVE already ran in the VBL; this second one exists only
   2463  f79b							; for slot 1's own fine adjust. HMP0/HMM0/HMBL still hold the PLAYER's,
   2464  f79b							; the laser's and the ball's fine values, and HMOVE would apply them a
   2465  f79b							; second time — the player's fine adjust doubled (drawn X advanced 2 px per
   2466  f79b							; 1 px of RoomX, sawing +/-15 px as the fine value cycled: the "raft
   2467  f79b							; zig-zag", user 2026-10-22). Clear them; HMP1 stays (set above).
   2468  f79b							; THESE CLEARS MUST SIT BEFORE THE `sta WSYNC` BELOW: they cost ~14 cycles,
   2469  f79b							; and an HMOVE written after cycle 0 of HBLANK gives up part of the fine
   2470  f79b							; shift (late-HMOVE penalty) — slot 1's sprite then snaps in ~4 px steps
