   2741  f945							; --- Cell walk (cell_collision_plan 2.1): test the PF buffers directly ---
   2742  f945							; The ZP rect cache ($CC-$DF, 5-slot limit) is gone from THIS walker: the
   2743  f945							; render buffers PF0/1/2Buf ARE the map (BombMarkWalls punches bomb holes
   2744  f945							; into them), so room complexity is unbounded and geometry parity is proven
   2745  f945							; by tools/test_cell_map.py (box vs geometry, all models/rooms).
   2746  f945							; Prologue ranges (all left-half space): CollisionCellY = top row,
   2747  f945							; CollisionEndY = bottom row, CollisionEndX = min col, CollisionCellX = max
   2748  f945							; col — cols are endpoint-mirrored above, so ALWAYS 0-19 here (no in-loop
   2749  f945							; mirror; bank2 display-space walkers add their own when they convert).
   2750  f945							; RectCount = running row, CollisionX = running col (both were walk temps
   2751  f945							; before — same ZP, no new allocation).
   2752  f945							; Exits: HIT -> jmp HotOverlapFlag (tail, C=1 contract preserved);
   2753  f945							;	  miss -> clc / rts. Stack depth during the walk = old walk exactly
   2754  f945							;	  (no jsr added — sim_bomb_fuse gameplay min-SP guard stays $F8).
