   2807  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2808  f97a							; E4 moth exit tramp ($FC49-$FC4E) — bank2 executes `sta $1FF4` at $FC49
   2809  f97a							; (byte-identical slice, guard: verify_build), then the fetch at $FC4C comes
   2810  f97a							; from bank0 = `jmp UE_Next` (real label here — no cross-bank address sync).
   2811  f97a							; bank0's `sta $1FF4` copy never runs; bank2's bytes from $FC4C never run.
   2812  f97a							;
   2813  f97a							; MUST stay off $FFF6-$FFF9: those are the ONLY addresses in code space where
   2814  f97a							; (addr & $1FFF) lands in $1FF4-$1FF7 = F6 hotspot mirrors. Stella's
   2815  f97a							; CartridgeEnhanced::peek (CartEnh.cxx:157, ADDR_MASK=$1FFF) calls
   2816  f97a							; checkSwitchBank on READS — the old $FFF2 placement fetched the `jmp`
   2817  f97a							; operands at $FFF6/$FFF7 and flipped banks mid-instruction (operand hi from
   2818  f97a							; bank1 = $00 -> jmp $007D -> HUD runaway, 359/360-line frames, 5-byte stack
   2819  f97a							; leak per rogue Overscan entry -> SP decayed to $E1 -> frame-3 crash where
   2820  f97a							; jsr RefreshEnemyY's return landed on FetchPtr). Real F6 is write-only, but
   2821  f97a							; no fetched byte may ever sit in the mirror zone.
   2822  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2823  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2824  f97a							; Cross-bank call pads (docs/leaf_move_plan.md) — byte-identical copies live in
   2825  f97a							; bank1 at the SAME addresses. F6 hotspots switch on ANY write — the written
   2826  f97a							; value is ignored (proven by FoldIndirect's `sta $1FF4` carrying data bytes) —
   2827  f97a							; so the pads `sta $1FF5`/`sta $1FF4` with A AS-IS: A/X/Y/flags pass through
   2828  f97a							; unchanged, making the pad equivalent to the original inlined `jsr`.
   2829  f97a							; (2026-09-30 bug: `lda #1` before `sta $1FF5` clobbered A — ClearPFColumn
   2830  f97a							; punched col 1 instead of the bomb's col, AddScore added +1 instead of
   2831  f97a							; +50/+75. Hole appeared at screen col 1 + mirror col 18 = "second tile from
   2832  f97a							; each edge"; collision stayed correct because WallMask is separate.)
   2833  f97a							; `sta` does not touch flags — IsRoomDark's `beq` contract survives the
   2834  f97a							; return. Carry survives. No stack use.
   2835  f97a							; ==============================================================================
   2836  f97a		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$F9B8 - *, 0	; Phase 4 overlay tramp — shared address with
   2837  f9b8							; bank2's twin image (40B bank2 hole before
   2838  f9b8							; org $F9D9); F6-safe ($F9B1 & $1FFF ∉ hotspots)
   2839  f9b8				   OverlayTramp
   2840  f9b8		       a5 84		      lda	LineCount	; packed asym byte (0 = symmetric)
   2841  f9ba		       f0 03		      beq	.OTsym	; sym: clc/rts, never enters the cluster
   2842  f9bc		       4c 2d fa 	      jmp	PHMOverlay	; bank0 cluster ($FA30; repack chunk 4)
   2843  f9bf				   .OTsym
   2844  f9bf		       18		      clc
   2845  f9c0		       60		      rts
