   3765  fda9							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3766  fda9							; BuildColupF — 12-byte final COLUPF image at ColupfBuf ($E7-$F2).
   3767  fda9							;   Stripe: rows 0,2 = LevelWallColor; row 1 = LevelWallColor2.
   3768  fda9							;   Hot rows overwrite with TickCounter-bit4 pulse (COLOR_HOT_Y/R).
   3769  fda9							;   $F0-$F2 (bombs) NO LONGER overlap-saved: body writes rows 0-2 only,
   3770  fda9							;   save/restore round trip deleted (S3.0b — window audit: zero writers).
   3771  fda9							;   Bank1 clobbers $E0-$EF during HUD; VBLANK rebuilds every frame.
   3772  fda9							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3773  fda9							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3774  fda9							; BuildColupF — MOVED to bank2 (S5.1) — CallPad_BuildColupF.
   3775  fda9							;   Hot-rect data (RoomRects) lives in bank2, so the body reads it with
   3776  fda9							;   direct (FetchPtr),Y — the shared $FEF6 fold block's sta $1FF4 always
   3777  fda9							;   returns to bank0, so a fold inside a bank1 body could not work.
   3778  fda9							;   The dark check is inlined there too: CallPad_IsRoomDark cannot nest
   3779  fda9							;   from a pad body (ReturnPad switches to bank0 mid-call).
   3780  fda9							;   Body: bank2.asm, pinned at $FC4F. Entry save block ($F0-$F2 → collision
   3781  fda9							;   temps) was dead (rows 0-2 only) — deleted with the .AfterRows restore
   3782  fda9							;   in S3.0b.
   3783  fda9							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3784  fda9
   3785  fda9							; UpdateBombSound moved to bank1 (leaf_move_plan batch A) — CallPad_UpdateBombSound.
   3786  fda9
   3787  fda9							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3788  fda9							; ColOff/ColMask — cell-walk lookup tables (cell_collision_plan).
   3789  fda9							;   Indexed by LEFT-HALF source col 0-19 (PHM prologue mirrors right-half
   3790  fda9							;   ranges before the walk; bank2 display-space walkers mirror first too).
   3791  fda9							;   ColOff: byte offset from PF0Buf+row ($C3+row) to the register holding
   3792  fda9							;   that col (0/3/6 = PF0/PF1/PF2 row byte). ColMask: the col's bit in that
   3793  fda9							;   byte — PF0 bit4+col (cols 0-3), PF1 MSB-first (4-11), PF2 LSB-first
   3794  fda9							;   (12-19); matches convert_room.pf_values (plan 0.2 spec, proven by
   3795  fda9							;   tools/test_cell_map.py).
   3796  fda9							;   (The standalone CellSolid leaf that lived here moved INTO
   3797  fda9							;   PlayerHitsMap's walk as inline code — a jsr in the walk cost 2B of
   3798  fda9							;   stack depth and would break sim_bomb_fuse's gameplay min-SP >= $F8
   3799  fda9							;   guard; the post-pad slot keeps these tables abs,X-reachable.)
   3800  fda9							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3801  fda9		       00 00 00 00*ColOff     .byte.b	0,0,0,0, 3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3, 6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6
   3802  fdbd		       10 20 40 80*ColMask    .byte.b	$10,$20,$40,$80,$80,$40,$20,$10,$08,$04,$02,$01
   3803  fdc9		       01 02 04 08*	      .byte.b	$01,$02,$04,$08,$10,$20,$40,$80
   3804  fdd1
   3805  fdd1							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3806  fdd1							; BombEnemyBlast — bank2 entry tramp ($FDD8, lamp-safe S9 2026-10-07): the
   3807  fdd1							; BombTick `jsr` lands here (bank0), `sta $1FF6` switches to bank2, the `jmp`
   3808  fdd1							; is fetched from bank2's byte-identical mirror at this same address and
   3809  fdd1							; lands on the body at $FD87 (the lamp type-check reads enemy records that
   3810  fdd1							; live in bank2). Body tail-jmps ReturnPad ($FBF8); A = 1 kill (BombTick
   3811  fdd1							; awards +50 — pads cannot nest), 0 none. Old inline body ($F87F, 66B)
   3812  fdd1							; deleted: the region re-packs into the gap before the $FBD6 fold pin
   3813  fdd1							; (pre-pad headroom stays 1B — pins absorb upstream shrink, not the org).
